<h2 id="define-websockets">Define Websockets</h2>

<p>Websockets are a communication protocol that is considered to be an upgrade over HTTP. The main catch with websockets is, unlike
traditional HTTP connections where after a client receives a response from a request it make to a server, the server closes 
the connection. There are other techniques of keeping the connection alive but as I studied more into Websockets and HTTP 
protocols, I got to know this ‘keep-alive’ state set for HTTP protocols may have its downsides.</p>

<p>Hope to cover more on that, back to websockets, The entire idea behind websockets is once a connection is created with the server,
there is bi-directional, full-duplex communication link established. This comes with the perk of being low-latent. Low latency in
computer networks mean there is minimal delay in processing volumes of data messages. Hence its suitable for online multiplayer
games, chat applications, sports or financial applications where change in data should be readily available to users/clients.</p>

<h2 id="more">More</h2>

<p>Unlike HTTP, Websockets also have their url scheme which helps identify websocket connections.
